        <mxCell id="_y_0K9D7F8i-KXrYn6BL-27" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Satge 1: Fetching the data&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each data provider instance is asked to produce a data set. Since instances are independent from oneanother, data provider instances work in parallel as much as the system allows.&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="40" width="670" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_y_0K9D7F8i-KXrYn6BL-28" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Satge 2: Storing data into an in-memory database&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Once all data providers have finished fetching their respective data sets, the data from each data set is uploaded into a new ephemeral in-memory database. A separate table is created for each data set.&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="200" width="670" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="_y_0K9D7F8i-KXrYn6BL-29" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Satge 3: Data crunching stage&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;An SQL statement is executed on the in-memory database. This handles any and all data crunching operations, such as joining, filtering, arithmetics, aggregation, sorting, producing of virtual records and re-arranging the data in any and every way. The data set resulted from running this SQL statement is returned to the user.&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="360" width="670" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
